// c-pattern-05: Reach::new decides `wildcard` before narrowing: an
// all-bind tuple arm leaves a coverage hole.
// Command: graphix --no-cache --no-fusion c-pattern-05.gx  (and --check)
// `g` passes --check. `(a, b)` probes as matching every member before
// the narrowing binds its cells to the first member, (i64, string), so
// `exhausted` trusts a stale `wildcard`.
// Expected: refused at --check ("no arm covers (string, i64)"), as the
// same select is once the union gains a `null` member (matched by a
// `null as _` arm), or (0, 0) if `(a, b)` were to match both members.
// Observed: --check exits 0; the run logs
//   select p { (a, b) => 0 }: no arm matches ["s", i64:1]: a coverage hole in the check
// and prints nothing (the tuple is bottom); both engines agree.
// The same select with a second `(c, d) => 1` arm is accepted
// and prints (0, 1): the per-arm reach after narrowing is right, only
// the wildcard verdict is stale.
let g = |p: [(i64, string), (string, i64)]| select p {
  (a, b) => 0
};
sys::exit(sys::time::after_idle(duration:100.ms, 0));
(g((1, "s")), g(("s", 1)))
